From b613e77cc4c470c6cda0accc3ab64129ee5dd012 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ferdinand Vanmaele <ferdinand-joseph.vanmaele@uni-a.de>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 23:50:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [clangd] workspace/symbol: rank mid-word matches by shape
 (middleMatch)

With middleMatch, a fuzzy match scattered over word starts ranked before
every mid-word one: "ector" listed Kokkos's EBOBaseImpl<T, true,
CtorNotOnDevice> constructor (E + Ctor) before any Vector, whose match
starts inside the word.  Matches now rank in two tiers.  The first holds
those whose query runs contiguously from a word start of the identifier,
scored and ordered as before.  The second holds the scattered fuzzy and
the mid-word matches, scored by the share of the identifier the query
covers, doubled when the match ends a word segment, or by the fuzzy
score if higher; so "Vector" comes before "AlignedVectorCopyConstruct".

Dex and MemIndex rank the same way, since their own cut at the limit
runs before getWorkspaceSymbols ranks.  A second-tier score becomes
-1 / (1 + score), below every first-tier one and in order.  Before, Dex
and MemIndex multiplied -1 by the symbol's quality, so among mid-word
matches the better symbol ranked lower and a limit kept the worst, and
getWorkspaceSymbols subtracted 1e6, which leaves steps of 0.0625 in a
float, so mid-word matches tied.

Without middleMatch (code completion) nothing changes.  Measured on a
deal.II / Kokkos / Trilinos index (emacs-cpp spike S15): no first-tier
match moved, the same matches found, replies as fast.
